  "davandeh|1984": {"id":213938,"poster":"/guwFSx1dEbELubxFuJIyMyj6NG0.jpg","title":"دونده","title_en":"The Runner","overview_en":"A young orphan named Amiro lives alone in an abandoned tanker in the Iranian port city of Abadan. He survives by shining shoes, selling water, and collecting deposit bottles. Although he sometimes finds himself at odds with both adults and competing older kids, he finds solace in dreams about departing cargo ships and airplanes—and by running.","kind":"movie","genre_ids":[18],"vote_average":7.224,"vote_count":38,"imdb_id":"tt0088992","rt_critic":100,"rt_url":"https://www.rottentomatoes.com/m/the_runner_1984","imdb_rating":7.6,"imdb_votes":2470},
  "dawn chorus もういちどみつめる|2025": {"id":1537786,"poster":"/qyaugNnxAvGGmJoGfwz8UZik6xr.jpg","title":"もういちどみつめる","title_en":"Dawn Chorus","overview_en":"Taciturn Yuki is our prickly protagonist. An 18-year-old who served time at a juvenile reformatory, after returning to the care of his father,his longing for a mother he barely knew and his frustrations push him to leave home and retrace his memories to a mountain forest where his aunt Noriko lives at a mountain campsite. It was there, as a child, that Yuki witnessed a creature he couldn’t identify amidst the trees at dawn, something which left him sensitive to the various presences in the world. It is there he hopes that reconnecting with his past may bring a sense of peace. Meanwhile, Noriko and the other adults around him become increasingly frustrated trying to understand what Yuki is thinking.","kind":"movie","genre_ids":[18],"vote_average":0,"vote_count":0},
  "dear tomorrow 拝啓アシタ|2025": {"id":1422637,"poster":"/n9FpYngV0gpIav5UWY24QoBWQpP.jpg","title":"拝啓アシタ","title_en":"Dear Tomorrow","overview_en":"Dear Tomorrow is a multi-character story about loneliness. Set in Japan, the film centers around the mental health hotline called “A Place for You”, where a group of young volunteers are chatting with thousands in need, every single day.","kind":"movie","genre_ids":[99],"vote_average":7.5,"vote_count":2,"imdb_id":"tt35520240","rt_url":"https://www.rottentomatoes.com/m/dear_tomorrow"},
  "dear tomorrow|2025": {"id":1422637,"poster":"/n9FpYngV0gpIav5UWY24QoBWQpP.jpg","title":"拝啓アシタ","title_en":"Dear Tomorrow","overview_en":"Dear Tomorrow is a multi-character story about loneliness. Set in Japan, the film centers around the mental health hotline called “A Place for You”, where a group of young volunteers are chatting with thousands in need, every single day.","kind":"movie","genre_ids":[99],"vote_average":7.5,"vote_count":2,"imdb_id":"tt35520240","rt_url":"https://www.rottentomatoes.com/m/dear_tomorrow"},
  "deep frame|2026": {"id":222825,"poster":null,"title":"The Frames: In the Deep Shade","title_en":"The Frames: In the Deep Shade","overview_en":"In The Deep Shade is a feature length film about The Frames.  Filmmaker Conor Masterson worked closely with the band over 18 months, beginning on their 20th anniversary tour in 2010.  'The Frames have always been very positive collaborators. I felt this was an opportunity to make a film that could explore their creativity as people and musicians as well as capturing some of their very dynamic and exciting live performances in close up.'","kind":"movie","genre_ids":[10402],"vote_average":0,"vote_count":0,"imdb_id":"tt2474156","rt_url":"https://www.rottentomatoes.com/m/the_frames_in_the_deep_shade/","imdb_rating":8.3,"imdb_votes":36},
